{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GwHBFLQUTTBxtdcubXHWLH","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel02.0-uc004-basename\n     2→title: \"Strip directory and suffix from filenames via basename\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator invokes the Go basename binary with file paths to extract the filename\n     6→  component, optionally removing a suffix. The differential testing harness runs both\n     7→  the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gbasename from coreutils) with the\n     8→  same arguments and compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n     9→\n    10→actor: Human Operator\n    11→\n    12→trigger: |\n    13→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd015-basename.yaml) and invokes do-work to\n    14→  produce a passing differential test for cmd/basename.\n    15→\n    16→flow:\n    17→  - id: F1\n    18→    step: |\n    19→      The operator runs \"./bin/basename /usr/bin/sort\". basename strips the directory\n    20→      prefix and prints \"sort\" followed by a newline.\n    21→  - id: F2\n    22→    step: |\n    23→      The operator runs \"./bin/basename include/stdio.h .h\". basename strips the\n    24→      directory prefix and removes the \".h\" suffix, printing \"stdio\".\n    25→  - id: F3\n    26→    step: |\n    27→      The operator runs \"./bin/basename -a /usr/bin/sort /usr/bin/cat\" to process\n    28→      multiple paths. basename prints \"sort\" and \"cat\" on separate lines.\n    29→  - id: F4\n    30→    step: |\n    31→      The operator runs \"./bin/basename -s .h include/stdio.h include/stdlib.h\" to\n    32→      strip a suffix from multiple paths. basename prints \"stdio\" and \"stdlib\".\n    33→  - id: F5\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/basename\n    36→      and gbasename with the same arguments and environment.\n    37→  - id: F6\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte and exit codes. Both binaries must\n    40→      produce identical output.\n    41→\n    42→touchpoints:\n    43→  - T1: \"cmd/basename — path stripping, suffix removal, multi-argument mode, NUL output (prd015-basename R1, R2, R3)\"\n    44→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, stdout comparison\"\n    45→\n    46→success_criteria:\n    47→  - id: S1\n    48→    criterion: cmd/basename compiles and ./bin/basename exists after mage build.\n    49→  - id: S2\n    50→    criterion: |\n    51→      \"./bin/basename /usr/bin/sort\" produces \"sort\", matching gbasename.\n    52→  - id: S3\n    53→    criterion: |\n    54→      Suffix removal works: \"./bin/basename include/stdio.h .h\" produces \"stdio\".\n    55→  - id: S4\n    56→    criterion: |\n    57→      Multi-argument mode works: \"-a\" processes each path independently.\n    58→  - id: S5\n    59→    criterion: |\n    60→      Edge cases match: root path (\"/\"), trailing slashes, empty string all produce\n    61→      output identical to gbasename.\n    62→  - id: S6\n    63→    criterion: |\n    64→      The differential test passes for simple paths, suffix removal, -a, -s, -z,\n    65→      root, trailing slashes, and empty string.\n    66→\n    67→out_of_scope:\n    68→  - Encoding-specific path handling is not tested; paths are byte sequences with \"/\" as separator.\n    69→  - NUL-delimited output (-z) is tested for byte correctness but not for consumption by\n    70→    downstream tools (xargs -0).\n    71→\n    72→test_suite: test-rel02.0\n    73→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a9d5fb3-6be8-4467-833b-a377d2483dda","uuid":"cc4d9a75-e10d-43cc-b370-be26aa0741e4","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/333/docs/specs/use-cases/rel02.0-uc004-basename.yaml","content":"id: rel02.0-uc004-basename\ntitle: \"Strip directory and suffix from filenames via basename\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator invokes the Go basename binary with file paths to extract the filename\n  component, optionally removing a suffix. The differential testing harness runs both\n  the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gbasename from coreutils) with the\n  same arguments and compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd015-basename.yaml) and invokes do-work to\n  produce a passing differential test for cmd/basename.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"./bin/basename /usr/bin/sort\". basename strips the directory\n      prefix and prints \"sort\" followed by a newline.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"./bin/basename include/stdio.h .h\". basename strips the\n      directory prefix and removes the \".h\" suffix, printing \"stdio\".\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"./bin/basename -a /usr/bin/sort /usr/bin/cat\" to process\n      multiple paths. basename prints \"sort\" and \"cat\" on separate lines.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"./bin/basename -s .h include/stdio.h include/stdlib.h\" to\n      strip a suffix from multiple paths. basename prints \"stdio\" and \"stdlib\".\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/basename\n      and gbasename with the same arguments and environment.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte and exit codes. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/basename — path stripping, suffix removal, multi-argument mode, NUL output (prd015-basename R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, stdout comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/basename compiles and ./bin/basename exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: |\n      \"./bin/basename /usr/bin/sort\" produces \"sort\", matching gbasename.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: |\n      Suffix removal works: \"./bin/basename include/stdio.h .h\" produces \"stdio\".\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      Multi-argument mode works: \"-a\" processes each path independently.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: |\n      Edge cases match: root path (\"/\"), trailing slashes, empty string all produce\n      output identical to gbasename.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test passes for simple paths, suffix removal, -a, -s, -z,\n      root, trailing slashes, and empty string.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Encoding-specific path handling is not tested; paths are byte sequences with \"/\" as separator.\n  - NUL-delimited output (-z) is tested for byte correctness but not for consumption by\n    downstream tools (xargs -0).\n\ntest_suite: test-rel02.0\n","numLines":73,"startLine":1,"totalLines":73}}}
